  "resultText": "`GET /reports/no-shows?from=...&to=...` now works. `npm test` passes (34 unit tests, 7 e2e), and `typecheck` and `lint` are clean.\n\n**Response:** an array of `{ practitionerId, noShows, feesCents }`, ordered by practitioner. It is empty when the period has no no-shows.\n\n**Design:** no-shows live in scheduling and fees live in billing, and the contexts only talk through events. So I added a separate `reporting` module with its own read-model table (`ReportingNoShow`, a new Prisma model), fed by events. I also made two changes to the contracts and billing:\n- **`AppointmentNoShow`:** it now carries `practitionerId`.\n- **New billing event:** `src/contracts/billing.events.ts` defines `NoShowFeeCharged`. `InvoicingService.chargeNoShow` now publishes it after issuing the fee invoice, so its constructor takes an `EventEmitter2` and the existing spec is updated.\n\n**Choices to check:**\n- **Period:** it is measured on the appointment's start time, with `from` inclusive and `to` exclusive. A date-only `to` such as `2026-03-31` therefore leaves out that day.\n- **Validation:** missing or unparseable `from`/`to` returns 400. A period where `from` isn't before `to` returns 422 (`InvalidReportPeriodError`).\n- **Event order:** the report gives the same result whichever of the no-show or fee event arrives first.\n- **Existing data:** only no-shows marked after this change appear in the report. Earlier ones aren't backfilled.\n- **Database:** the new table needs `npm run db:push` on a real database. The e2e setup does it automatically.\n\nThe new unit tests are in `src/modules/reporting/application/no-show-report.service.spec.ts` and the billing spec. The e2e tests are in `test/clinic-flow.e2e-spec.ts`. I haven't committed anything.",
